question Aux is new on Aux, which is new too, and Update SolidWorks adds a gear only on a shaft the layout part has, so the gearbox needs building again. Shaft Aux is new, and the layout part has no axis for it. Gear_m1.25_N29 (Sun): Flank changed from involute to arcs, which its values cannot carry, so it needs a new part. Build again as RangeBox_r2? That makes new parts for Sun (Gear_m1.25_N29_r2) and Aux (Gear_m1.25_N20), reuses 4 parts that have not changed and makes a new layout part, carrier part and assembly (RangeBox_r2_Layout, RangeBox_r2_Carrier_Carrier and RangeBox_r2.SLDASM). Nothing is overwritten, and RangeBox.SLDASM stays as it is on disk, but it shares the 4 reused parts: a later Update SolidWorks that changes one of them changes RangeBox.SLDASM too. Gear Generator has not yet been shown to carry your work into a new revision on SolidWorks 2026 (findings.CARRY_INSERTS_ON_2026), so as read at 03:18, your Sprocket-2, Sprocket-4, Sprocket-1, 14 other components and 31 mates stay in RangeBox.SLDASM, and your User Keyway Sketch and User Keyway stay in Gear_m1.25_N29, which Sun's new part replaces; RangeBox_r2 has none of them, nor anything added since.
