status  (carry, after the build) Built 2 parts, RangeBox_r2_Layout, RangeBox_r2_Carrier_Carrier and RangeBox_r2.SLDASM, reusing the 4 parts already built; no interference between the gears in any mode, where they stand. Its turning gears are mated to turn in each of its 3 modes, one configuration each (H, N and L), and SolidWorks reports no mate in error in any of them: it opens in H; to switch mode, double-click another mode's configuration in SolidWorks' ConfigurationManager. Drag Sun in SolidWorks and the rest of its train follow. RangeSlv slides along Output, to its place in each mode. The 3 copies of Planet turn on Carrier, and RangeBox_r2_Carrier_Carrier holds Carrier's axes and planes only: a plate and pins are yours to add. Ring stays fixed where it is placed: its shaft does not turn. A turn you give the gears in one mode can show in other modes, so a dog can stand across its sleeve in another; to put the gears back there, press Update SolidWorks with that mode showing. 1 thing to do by hand: Assign a material to each of the 2 parts; the build leaves it unset. Carried into RangeBox_r2, unsaved: your Housing-1, Sprocket-1, Sprocket-2 and 14 other components, each where it stood, and 25 of your 31 mates, each on in the modes it was on in. UserAsm6 is on a plane of RangeBox.SLDASM itself, which Gear Generator did not read while SprocketLight-1 was lightweight in it, so it is not made again. UserAxis9 is on Sprocket-9, which is suppressed in H, the mode RangeBox.SLDASM showed, so it could not be read and is not made again. UserSunFace was on a face of Sun, and Sun's part is new because its Flank changed, so it is not made again. UserGearFillet was on a face of Sun, and Sun's part is new because its Flank changed, so it is not made again. UserAxisLight is on SprocketLight-1, which was lightweight in RangeBox.SLDASM, so what it joins could not be read, and it is not made again. Your User Keyway Sketch and User Keyway stay in Gear_m1.25_N29, which Sun's new part replaces because its Flank changed (RangeBox.SLDASM and that file keep them). Housing-1 and Sprocket-9 are fixed where they stood in RangeBox_r2: with your UserLock8a made again SolidWorks reads Sun unable to turn, so it was not kept; UserAngle8b beside it was. Your components were placed where they stood in H, the mode RangeBox.SLDASM showed; one no mate holds stands there in every mode. Assembly features, display states and appearances stay behind; sub-assemblies come over rigid, pattern instances as components of their own. If a part of yours was made in context of RangeBox.SLDASM, it still refers to that assembly's parts. SprocketLight-1 was lightweight in RangeBox.SLDASM and is resolved there now: SolidWorks loaded its part to carry it. Save RangeBox_r2 in SolidWorks to keep what was carried.
